use p4flat picks its encode implementation\n            # (GPU vs CPU) from the producer mode below.\n            #\n            #   gpu_direct:\n            #       Backend's existing pipeline produces compressed KV on GPU\n            #       (DietGPU/MantExp/p4flat run compress kernels on\n            #       comp_stream).  Raw secondary unload runs in parallel.\n            #\n            #   cpu_after_raw_swap:\n            #       Avoid GPU compression entirely.  Raw KV is D2H'd to\n            #       LPDDR secondary first, then a CPU compressor reads\n            #       directly from secondary_kv (no extra D2H) and writes\n            #       into the persistent compressed host pool.  Supported only\n            #       by backends that ship a CPU encoder: ZipServ (C++ worker\n            #       manager), p4flat, and ChunkDelta3 (Python worker boundary\n            #       around an OpenMP C++ encoder).\n            # Default is backend-aware.  ZipServ is CPU-encode only in the\n            # serving path: raw KV is first swapped to secondary_kv and its C++\n            # worker manager compresses directly from that host tensor.  This\n            # is also enforced below so an inherited producer env cannot route\n            # ``--kv-comp zipserv`` back through gpu_direct.  GPU-kernel\n            # backends (dietgpu / mantexp / p4flat) default to gpu_direct.\n            # ``p4flatcpu`` is the explicit CPU-encode (C++ OpenMP\n            # host_encode_blocks) variant of the p4flat codec — it always uses\n            # the cpu_after_raw_swap producer, regardless of the env default.\n            # p4flat's gpu_direct compress runs 3 device kernels\n            # (compress_lean) on comp_stream.  When weight compression is also\n            # active, those kernels contend with weight-decompress + fused-mm\n            # GEMM for SMs — measured +~51ms GPUFwd (an un-attributed forward\n            # gap = the compress kernels) and +~25ms stall, a 1.26x slowdow